Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 18:35:19 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 069/111] script: IScene's camera, initial configs and
 timelines; ICamera

- IScene.getCameraTransforms / setCameraTransforms (a CameraTransforms: camera.eye/center/up and
  general.zoom; a 3D scene's view follows from the next frame), getInitialLayerConfig (the layer's
  object as the scene file has it: the scene's file name is kept now, it was ""), getAnimation (a
  keyframe timeline by name). createModelData / destroyModelData exist and build nothing (LWE makes no
  meshes from script data; no library scene does). renderContext is defined (an empty interface).
- A camera object's ICamera zoom / fov are layer properties (read, written, scripted).
- IAnimation.fps is the timeline's fps (30, not 29.999998 from 1 / (1 / 30)).

Origin: ours
Why: docs/player/spikes/we-coverage.md (SceneScript coverage)
Status: candidate-for-upstream
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
